  "reproduction_notes": [
    "No earlier generated output is an input to either control; both can be run independently from the listed sources.",
    "The generated .tm files and DAGs are deterministic in the tested runtime. The mp_birth results ledger embeds input paths relative to the driver directory parent, so changing the driver directory basename changes those metadata strings.",
    "Each driver overwrites generated measurements only in its own output directory; Python may also create import caches. Record any desired prior output before rerunning.",
    "Every emitted working state has both read-symbol rows. The original missing backend row is explicitly totalized by preserving the read bit, moving right, and halting.",
    "The complete source counts are relative to the 281-state public Wade baseline and cannot be subtracted from the separately optimized 252-state decoder.",
    "Finite source-path controls and source decision re-extraction do not establish a new compiled blank-tape simulation theorem or consistency endpoint."
  ],
